# ComposeUX — The Menu-Indexed Screen Resolver [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

> A generic engine: given a structured menu TREE, a filesystem ROOT, and a naming CONVENTION, resolve any menu node to an asset reference — deriving its path, never storing it, walking a defined fallback chain when the node's own art is absent, and linting the tree and the art directory into bidirectional agreement. The engine carries no BSG, HELM, amber, or SVG-slot vocabulary ([DX-ENGINE-VS-POLICY]); BSG's Colonial Console (`cic_menu`) is documented here as instance #1 — SCOPED to STD's per-(console, sub-tab) grid, riding the engine by reference rather than forking it ([DX-NARROW-WAIST]). Mode selection and mode-surface resolution are a DIFFERENT, adjacent tier this instance does not model (§5). Section 6 captures several related [SPEC:CXC-COMP] extensions David raised in the same review pass, each filed `part-of: [SPEC:CXC-COMP]`; it is POLICY, not engine, content. ✅ **[PLACEMENT RATIFIED]** (David, DSD 2026-08-18, `docs/architecture/DECISIONS-menu-resolver-forks.md`, [DEC-CXC-MENU-SPEC-HOME-NEW-DOC]) — filed as a new numbered doc (77), per the [DD-COMP-SPEC-HOME] precedent (one-slice-per-numbered-doc). Section 6's physical migration to [SPEC:CXC-COMP] is a ratified FOLLOW-ON, not a landing blocker — see [DD-MENU-SPEC-HOME].

---

## 1. Intent & the engine/policy seam

### [CXC-MENU-WHY] The engine/policy seam for menu-indexed screen resolution

- definition: [CXC-COMP-STD-CONTENT] already resolves STD's per-(console, sub-tab) screens by reference, and `composite.py`'s `MODE_FIXTURES` hand-maintains a parallel mode->file dict for the DIFFERENT mode-surface tier — two instances of the same shape (a menu-indexed lookup) built ad hoc rather than once. This spec extracts the GENERIC mechanism for the FORMER (any depth, any app), and explicitly does NOT fold the latter in (§5, [CXC-MENU-CIC-INSTANCE]'s `corrected` note) — the two tiers use different naming conventions and conflating them was an error caught in review, not a design choice.
- role: names the seam per [DX-ENGINE-VS-POLICY] — "what is the mechanism EVERY deployment needs vs. the policy only THIS one needs?" The mechanism (tree, slug, path derivation, walk, lint) is the GENERIC ENGINE (sections 2-4) and ports to any ComposeIO app. The policy (menu CONTENTS, the colonial theme, the actual SVGs, the `slot:@` vocabulary) stays in BSG (section 5). A builder MUST be able to read sections 2-4 without learning what HELM or DRADIS are.
- requirement: sections 2-4 ([CXC-MENU-SCHEMA] through [CXC-MENU-LINT]) MUST NOT reference a BSG-specific label, an SVG element name, or the `slot:@` grammar — including in their worked examples, not only their definitions; every BSG fact MUST live in section 5 and be cited from there. Section 6 is exempt from this rule by design: it is explicitly-marked [SPEC:CXC-COMP] policy content, not engine content.
- reuse-by-reference: the by-reference resolve + placeholder discipline is not reinvented — it generalizes [CXC-COMP-MISSING]'s screen-level "missing -> placeholder, never fall-through" ([DD-MENU-WALK-AMENDMENT] below proposes the one place this generalization changes behavior, not the principle). It deliberately does NOT touch [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]'s separate mode-level never-fall-through rule, which governs a tier this spec does not model. No fork.
- placement-status: "[PLACEMENT RATIFIED] (David, DSD 2026-08-18, [DEC-CXC-MENU-SPEC-HOME-NEW-DOC]). Filed as `corpora/platform-specs/77-composeux-menu-resolver.lts` — option (a) of [DD-MENU-SPEC-HOME], now the ratified home, per [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT]'s standing guard. `artifact-readiness: design-review` is UNCHANGED — the DESIGN is ratified; the ENGINE is not yet built, so nothing in this document authorizes a build."
- see-also: [DX-ENGINE-VS-POLICY], [DX-NARROW-WAIST]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

---

## 2. Generic engine contract — the menu schema

### [CXC-MENU-SCHEMA] The menu schema — the structured-data source of truth for a menu document

- definition: the menu is STRUCTURED DATA (YAML), the source of truth for the tree, superseding a hand-maintained markdown listing ([DD-MENU-SCHEMA-FORMAT] — settled). The schema carries exactly four things: a `root` (the filesystem root every derived path is relative to), an `extension` (the default asset file extension, no leading dot — app policy), a `bus-namespace` (the `bus://assets/<namespace>/...` segment a resolved reference publishes under), and a `tree` — a nested list of nodes, each carrying a `label` (the human-readable menu text; also the ONLY input to slug derivation, [CXC-MENU-SLUG]), an optional `children` (its absence or emptiness marks the node a LEAF), and an optional `annotation` ([CXC-MENU-ANNOTATION]).
- requirement: a menu document MUST declare exactly one `root`, one `extension`, and one `bus-namespace` at the top level, and MUST NOT declare a per-node `slug` field — the slug is DERIVED from `label` ([CXC-MENU-SLUG]), never authored, so the tree cannot silently diverge into a label that says one thing and a slug that says another. The SAME menu document MUST feed every consumer that needs the tree — a nav-row renderer, this resolver, a scaffolding tool, and the lint — so there is exactly one source, never a markdown copy plus a code copy.
- worked-shape: |
    root: /assets
    extension: png
    bus-namespace: demo
    tree:
      - label: Foo
        children:
          - {label: Bar}
          - {label: Baz}
      - label: Qux
        children:
          - {label: Log, annotation: {kind: pure-widget-no-file}}
- default: an unannotated leaf is treated as `kind: bespoke-svg` — the common case needs no annotation at all ([CXC-MENU-ANNOTATION]). (The token is spelled `bespoke-svg` for historical continuity with [CXC-COMP-KINDS]; the engine does not require the resolved file to actually be an SVG — `extension` decides that.)
- scenario:
  - when: a second ComposeIO app authors its own menu YAML with its own `root`/`extension`/`bus-namespace` and `tree`
  - then: it resolves through this SAME engine with zero code change — the engine reads no app-specific vocabulary, only the four schema fields above
- see-also: [DX-STRUCTURE-SURVIVES], [DX-A-NEW-FACT-IS-STATE-NEVER-A-HANDLER]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

### [CXC-MENU-SLUG] Slug derivation from a menu label

- definition: a node's slug is derived from its `label` by ONE deterministic rule, never authored, never stored: lowercase the label; collapse each run of one-or-more non-alphanumeric characters to a single hyphen; trim a leading or trailing hyphen left by a label that starts or ends on a non-alphanumeric run.
- requirement: the resolver MUST derive a slug from `label` on every read and MUST NOT accept or persist a separately-authored slug field ([CXC-MENU-SCHEMA]) — a value no human maintains cannot rot ([DX-A-NEW-FACT-IS-STATE-NEVER-A-HANDLER] applied to naming: the slug is a projection of the label, not a second fact to keep in sync). The derived slug MUST NOT equal the reserved token `default` — [CXC-MENU-WALK]'s ancestor-fallback sentinel filename stem, guarded by [CXC-MENU-LINT]'s `reserved-slug` check — because a leaf slugging to `default` would collide with its own would-be sibling fallback file and make the walk's own output ambiguous for that node's parent.
- default: two sibling nodes (same parent) whose labels collapse to the same slug is a lint ERROR (`slug-collision`, [CXC-MENU-LINT]), not a silently-resolved pick. A leaf whose label collapses to exactly `default` is a lint ERROR (`reserved-slug`, [CXC-MENU-LINT]) unless it carries an explicit `annotation.path` override supplying a distinct concrete filename.
- scenario:
  - when: labels "FOO BAR", "QUX-WIDGET!!", and "  BAZ" (leading whitespace) are each passed through the rule
  - then: they derive "foo-bar" (basic multi-word), "qux-widget" (trailing punctuation run collapsed and trimmed), and "baz" (leading run trimmed) respectively — no manual mapping table anywhere in the engine or the app. (BSG's own instance reproduces this rule against real labels in [CXC-MENU-CIC-INVENTORY]'s table.)
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-SCHEMA], [CXC-MENU-PATH], [CXC-MENU-WALK]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

### [CXC-MENU-ANNOTATION] The optional per-node annotation — the engine's escape hatch

- definition: an `annotation` block is the ESCAPE HATCH, not the mechanism — it carries ONLY what convention cannot derive. Two fields, both optional: `kind` (one of the three tokens in [CXC-MENU-KINDS]; absent = `bespoke-svg`) and `path` (a deliberate art-path OVERRIDE for a rare, intentional reuse/share; when present it REPLACES the derived path entirely — [CXC-MENU-PATH] never runs for that node).
- requirement: an app author MUST leave `annotation` absent for the common case (a leaf with its own convention-derived art); MUST supply `kind: pure-widget-no-file` or `kind: live-drop-in` for a leaf the lint should NOT expect a file for; and MUST supply `path` only for a genuine deliberate override — including the reserved-slug case ([CXC-MENU-SLUG]) — never as a substitute for fixing a label that derives the wrong slug.
- default: no annotation -> `kind: bespoke-svg`, no path override -> the derived path from [CXC-MENU-PATH].
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-KINDS], [CXC-MENU-PATH]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

---

## 3. Generic engine contract — resolution

### [CXC-MENU-PATH] Default asset-path derivation from a leaf's slug path

- definition: a leaf's DEFAULT art path is `<root>/<s1>/<s2>/.../<sn>.<extension>`, where `s1..sn` are the DERIVED slugs ([CXC-MENU-SLUG]) of every ancestor from the tree's top level down to and including the leaf itself. Nothing about this path is stored anywhere — it is recomputed from the tree on every resolve ([DX-A-NEW-FACT-IS-STATE-NEVER-A-HANDLER], P1B: derive when the node holds the inputs).
- requirement: the resolver MUST compute this path by walking the tree from the leaf to the root and joining derived slugs with `/`, and MUST NOT read it from, or write it to, any manifest, dict, or cache treated as a source of truth (a derivation cache for performance is permitted; it MUST NOT diverge from re-derivation, per [CXC-COMP-CREDO]'s no-second-copy discipline).
- generalizes: the join works identically for a tree of ANY depth — depth 1, depth 3, depth 10 are the same operation applied N times. This formula is a generalization of a concrete depth-3 convention one app already used by hand; see [CXC-MENU-CIC-INSTANCE] for that worked instance and for the one place the generalization required a correction, not an assumption.
- default: a node with an `annotation.path` override ([CXC-MENU-ANNOTATION]) uses that value instead of this derivation; every other node uses this derivation unconditionally.
- scenario:
  - when: the leaf `Foo > Bar > Baz` is resolved against `root: /assets`, `extension: png`
  - then: the derived path is `/assets/foo/bar/baz.png` — no app-specific code, only the ancestor-slug join
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-SLUG], [CXC-MENU-WALK]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

### [CXC-MENU-WALK] The fallback walk for an unresolved leaf

- definition: when a leaf's own derived (or overridden) path does not resolve to a real asset, the resolver walks OUTWARD through the leaf's ancestors, innermost first, trying `<root>/<s1>/.../<sk>/default.<extension>` for each ancestor depth `k` from `n-1` down to `1`; the first hit wins. Exhausting every ancestor without a hit yields the clean labeled placeholder ("`<full label path>` — screen not built"), never a fall-through to another leaf's resolved asset.
- change: "A missing leaf's art now falls back through its ANCESTORS' default backdrops before the placeholder, instead of going straight to the placeholder."
- context_for_change:
    prior_state: "[CXC-COMP-MISSING] (ratified): a missing/unbuilt (console, sub-tab) renders the clean placeholder directly — no intermediate fallback of any kind. That invariant is SCOPED to screen-level resolution; it does not touch [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]'s separate, UNCHANGED mode-level never-fall-through rule (a mode must never render another mode's content — this walk never crosses a top-level mode boundary, and does not model mode-level resolution at all, §5)."
    reasoning: "A shared ancestor-level backdrop is a more honest 'not built yet' than a bare placeholder for a leaf that has no distinctive art yet, and it lets a screen degrade gracefully while its own art is authored incrementally. The walk is bounded (never crosses the tree's own root) so it cannot become the fall-through-to-another-leaf defect [CXC-COMP-MISSING] exists to prevent."
    rejected_alternative: "Keep [CXC-COMP-MISSING] exactly as ratified — no walk, straight to placeholder always. This was the fallback if David rejected the amendment; he did not — David RATIFIED the walk via the DSD ([DEC-CXC-MENU-WALK-AMENDMENT-ADOPTED], `docs/architecture/DECISIONS-menu-resolver-forks.md`, 2026-08-18), so this alternative is now foreclosed."
    counter_argument: "A fallback walk is one more place a missing screen can silently look 'good enough' when it is not actually built, weakening the placeholder's honesty."
    counter_response: "The walk only ever resolves to an EXPLICITLY authored `default.<ext>` at an ancestor level — never an unrelated sibling's art — so it degrades to art someone deliberately provided as a fallback, not to a guess. Absent any `default.<ext>` at any ancestor, behavior is identical to today's [CXC-COMP-MISSING]."
    invalidating_assumption: "That an ancestor-level `default.<ext>` is a genuine authored asset and not itself missing. If no app ever authors one, the walk is a no-op and this amendment has no observable effect."
    implication: "[CXC-COMP-MISSING]'s placeholder rule is NOT repealed — it is the walk's terminal case. Its base/mode-ownership split and its scope over [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]'s mode-level rule are UNCHANGED and continue to govern; only the screen-level 'straight to placeholder' step gains optional intermediate stops."
- on-ratify: "[DD-MENU-WALK-AMENDMENT] IS NOW RATIFIED ([DEC-CXC-MENU-WALK-AMENDMENT-ADOPTED], David, DSD 2026-08-18) — the FIRST of the two gates on upgrading the Relationships section's `[CXC-MENU-WALK] RELATED_TO [CXC-COMP-MISSING]` edge to a typed AMENDS edge has now cleared. The SECOND gate has not: `AMENDS` is not yet a registered verb — it needs an `EDGETYPE-AMENDS` registration in `platform-composeio-profile.lts` (naming its `property-key`, mirroring how `[EDGETYPE-DOCUMENTS]` was registered per SPEC §1.3.2), which has not landed. Until it does, `RELATED_TO` stays the correct edge — minting a verb the parser cannot yet resolve would assert infrastructure that does not exist, which is worse than the weaker edge."
- requirement: the resolver MUST try, in strict inner-to-outer order, the leaf's own path, then each ancestor's `default.<extension>` from innermost to the tree's top level, and MUST NOT skip an intermediate level or invert the order; it MUST NOT ever return another LEAF's own resolved path as a fallback (only ancestor-level `default.<extension>` files are eligible); and reaching the end of the walk with no hit MUST yield the placeholder, never an error and never empty output.
- default: no `default.<extension>` authored at any ancestor level -> the walk degrades exactly to today's [CXC-COMP-MISSING] behavior (leaf miss -> placeholder, one step).
- scenario:
  - when: leaf `Foo > Bar` has no `bar.png`, but `/assets/foo/default.png` exists
  - then: the resolver returns `/assets/foo/default.png`, never the placeholder and never another leaf's asset
  - and: if `/assets/foo/default.png` were also absent, the walk tries `/assets/default.png`, then the placeholder
- see-also: [CXC-COMP-MISSING], [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE], [DD-MENU-WALK-AMENDMENT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

### [CXC-MENU-RESOLVE] Resolve — a menu node to a bus asset reference

- definition: `resolve(node)` composes [CXC-MENU-PATH] (or the `annotation.path` override) and [CXC-MENU-WALK] into one function returning a `bus://assets/<bus-namespace>/<slug-path>.<extension>` reference, publishing under the schema's declared `bus-namespace` ([CXC-MENU-SCHEMA]) — the resolve-by-reference model several bus-backed ComposeIO apps already use ad hoc, generalized here to any namespace.
- requirement: `resolve` MUST be a PURE function of the menu tree + the node identity (no hidden state, no cache treated as authoritative) and MUST return a `bus://` reference in every case — the leaf's own asset, a walked ancestor default, or the placeholder marker — never raise, never return nothing ([CXC-COMP-MISSING]'s drop-nothing discipline, generalized).
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-PATH], [CXC-MENU-WALK], [CXC-MENU-SCHEMA]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

### [CXC-MENU-KINDS] The screen-kind annotation vocabulary

- definition: three OPAQUE tokens the engine carries but does not interpret: `bespoke-svg` (a distinctive art file is expected at the leaf's own path), `pure-widget-no-file` (no file is ever expected — the leaf composes a generic widget directly), `live-drop-in` (no file is ever expected — the leaf mounts an existing self-contained live surface). The engine's ONLY use of `kind` is deciding, for the doc->tree lint ([CXC-MENU-LINT]), whether a leaf's missing own-file is a FINDING (`bespoke-svg`, file expected) or NOT (`pure-widget-no-file` / `live-drop-in`, no file ever expected) — it does not know what an SVG slot is, what a widget composition looks like, or what a live drop-in mounts.
- requirement: the lint MUST treat exactly `pure-widget-no-file` and `live-drop-in` as file-not-expected, and every other value (including absence, which defaults to `bespoke-svg`) as file-expected; an app author MUST NOT invent a fourth token in the engine layer — an app-specific rendering distinction belongs in the APP's own kind vocabulary (e.g. [CXC-COMP-KINDS]), not in this generic set.
- relates-to: [CXC-COMP-KINDS] is BSG's existing, richer (a)/(b)/(c) vocabulary for the SAME three-way split, carrying SVG-rendering semantics this engine layer deliberately does not know. The two are the SAME idea at two seams — [CXC-COMP-KINDS] is the policy-side interpretation of the tokens this engine treats as opaque. This spec does not modify or supersede [CXC-COMP-KINDS]; that consolidation, if wanted, is separate future work, not assumed here.
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-ANNOTATION], [CXC-MENU-LINT], [CXC-COMP-KINDS]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

---

## 4. Generic engine contract — the bidirectional lint

### [CXC-MENU-LINT] The bidirectional tree<->asset lint

- definition: the enforcement that makes "menu and art agree" a FACT rather than a claim ([CXC-MENU-SCHEMA]'s single-source premise is worthless without a check). FOUR checks over the SAME tree + the SAME filesystem scan in one pass — two WARNING (an incompleteness that leaves a leaf unresolved, but resolution stays well-defined) and two ERROR (a structural ambiguity that makes resolution UNDEFINED for the affected node(s)), mirroring [CXC-COMP-LINT]'s own ERROR/WARNING split:
  - (a) DOC -> TREE, WARNING, `unbuilt-and-undeclared`: every LEAF in the tree must satisfy at least one of — its own derived/overridden path resolves to a real file; OR its `annotation.kind` is `pure-widget-no-file` or `live-drop-in` ([CXC-MENU-KINDS], no file ever expected); OR the fallback walk ([CXC-MENU-WALK]) hits a real ancestor default. A leaf satisfying NONE of these is flagged, naming the leaf's full label path.
  - (b) TREE -> DOC, WARNING, `orphan`: every file matching `<root>/**/*.<extension>` must equal SOME leaf's own derived-or-overridden path in the CURRENT tree (an ancestor `default.<extension>` counts as accounted for too). A file matching neither is flagged, naming the file — this is the negative control that catches a renamed, typo'd, or deleted menu entry whose art was left behind.
  - (c) SIBLING-SLUG COLLISION, ERROR, `slug-collision`: two sibling nodes (same parent) whose labels derive the SAME slug ([CXC-MENU-SLUG]) make `resolve` ambiguous for BOTH — flagged naming the parent and both colliding labels. ERROR, not WARNING: this is not an incompleteness gap, it is a broken contract — two different menu entries would silently share one path.
  - (d) RESERVED-SLUG, ERROR, `reserved-slug`: a leaf whose derived slug equals `default` collides with [CXC-MENU-WALK]'s own ancestor-fallback sentinel filename stem — flagged naming the leaf. ERROR, for the same reason as (c): the leaf and its would-be sibling `default.<extension>` become indistinguishable.
- requirement: the lint MUST run all four checks over the SAME tree + the SAME filesystem scan in one pass (no drift between separate runs); MUST classify (a)/(b) as WARNING and (c)/(d) as ERROR, and MUST preserve the tree/file in every case — a WARNING never drops anything, and an ERROR still names and preserves what it flags, it only additionally REFUSES a publish/build gate the way [CXC-COMP-LINT]'s bake refuses on ERROR (matching [CXC-COMP-LINT]'s preserve-and-flag discipline and this corpus's forward+orphan dangle-lint precedent, `lts_lint(dangle=true)`); and an app author MUST be able to run it standalone (CLI/CI/bus-peer) exactly like [CXC-COMP-LINT]'s ONE-linter, N-front-ends discipline.
- default: a tree with every leaf either file-backed, kind-annotated as fileless, or walk-satisfied, no sibling-slug collisions, no leaf slugging to `default`, and an asset directory with no file outside the tree, lints CLEAN with zero findings across all four checks.
- scenario:
  - when: a leaf's label is renamed in the YAML from "Bar" to "Bar Prime" without renaming `bar.png` on disk
  - then: (a) flags "Foo / Bar Prime" as `unbuilt-and-undeclared` (its new slug `bar-prime` resolves to nothing) and (b) flags `foo/bar.png` as `orphan` (no current leaf's slug path matches it) — the SAME rename produces BOTH findings, catching it from either direction
- scenario:
  - when: two siblings under `Foo` are labelled "Bar!" and "Bar?" (both derive slug `bar`), and a third sibling is labelled "Default" (derives slug `default`)
  - then: (c) flags a `slug-collision` naming `Foo` and both `Bar!`/`Bar?`, and (d) flags a `reserved-slug` naming `Foo > Default` — both ERROR, both blocking a publish gate that runs this lint
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-RESOLVE], [CXC-MENU-WALK], [CXC-MENU-SLUG], [CXC-COMP-LINT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

---

## 5. BSG instance #1 — `cic_menu`, scoped to STD's grid

### [CXC-MENU-CIC-INSTANCE] BSG's `cic_menu` as resolver instance #1, scoped to STD's per-(console, sub-tab) grid

- definition: BSG's Colonial Console binds the generic schema concretely, SCOPED to STD's per-(console, sub-tab) grid — the ONLY tier this resolver instance covers: `root: compose_projects/bsg/resources/screen_base_layout/std` (the `std` segment is FOLDED INTO the root, since this instance resolves STD's content tree specifically), `extension: svg`, `bus-namespace: cic`. The tree's top level is STD's 7 CONSOLES ([CXC-MENU-CIC-INVENTORY]), each carrying its 5 SUB-TABS as leaves. Mode SELECTION (the radio row choosing STD/DRADIS/EXT/CHRONO, [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]) and mode-SURFACE resolution (each mode's own `<mode>_mode.svg` — including STD's own shell surface — today `composite.py`'s hand-maintained `MODE_FIXTURES` dict) are a DIFFERENT, SHALLOWER tier this resolver instance does NOT model: a mode-surface file resolves by a suffix convention (`<slug>_mode.svg`), not by the directory-join convention [CXC-MENU-PATH] derives, so folding a mode into THIS tree as a leaf would derive the WRONG path (`<root>/ext.svg`, not `ext_mode.svg`).
- corrected: "An earlier draft of this node listed STD/DRADIS/EXT/CHRONO as the tree's top level, with DRADIS/EXT/CHRONO each a single annotated leaf. Independent QA caught the contradiction: [CXC-MENU-PATH]'s own derivation formula cannot produce `ext_mode.svg` from a leaf named `EXT` — it would produce `ext.svg`. Fixed by scoping this instance to STD's grid only, folding `std` into `root`, and moving mode-surface resolution out of the tree entirely (below). Whether a FUTURE resolver instance — or a generalization of this one — also covers mode-surface resolution is left OPEN and explicitly OUT OF SCOPE here, not assumed."
- source-of-truth-supersession: this instance's tree SUPERSEDES `cic_menu_structure.md` as the menu's source of truth — [DD-MENU-SCHEMA-FORMAT] (settled, David decided). The same YAML is intended to feed the nav-row renderer, this resolver, a screen scaffolder, and [CXC-MENU-LINT]; the nav-row renderer's `menu.py` parser and BSG's publish step MUST migrate to read this YAML tree instead of `cic_menu_structure.md` — `cic_menu_structure.md` is retired once both consumers migrate, not before.
- measured-evidence-for-single-source: `compose_projects/bsg/resources/screen_base_layout/STD-screen-modeling-guidance.md`'s own appendix table (authored earlier, from the SAME markdown menu) lists NAVCON with only 3 sub-tabs (CARTOGRAPHY, PLOT, TAC); the current `cic_menu_structure.md` lists NAVCON with 5 (CARTOGRAPHY, DEAD REC, PLOT, TAC, ATTACK PT). The two documents describing "the same menu" have ALREADY drifted — measured, not hypothetical — which is exactly the failure a single structured source with one set of consumers is meant to close.
- flag-scope-of-mode-fixtures: `composite.py`'s `MODE_FIXTURES` dict (`{"STD": "std_mode.svg", "EXT": "ext_mode.svg", "DRADIS": "dradis_mode.svg"}`, CHRONO left unmapped) maps MODE LABEL to its mode-surface file. It is cited here only as the motivating instance of the SAME disease (a hand-maintained lookup dict standing in for a derivable convention, [DX-A-NEW-FACT-IS-STATE-NEVER-A-HANDLER]) that this spec corrects for the far more numerous 35-screen case — this spec does NOT retire it. CHRONO's silent absence from the dict — a mode that is "David's WIP" rendering as an undifferentiated placeholder with no signal distinguishing "not started" from "just never added to the dict" — is itself a `pure-manual-dict` failure mode this design's lint would catch immediately as `unbuilt-and-undeclared`, WERE CHRONO ever modeled as a tree leaf in a future mode-surface-covering instance; it is not one today.
- requirement: an app onboarding onto this engine MUST author its tree in the schema of [CXC-MENU-SCHEMA] and MUST NOT re-derive its own path-join or slug logic — BSG's instance is the worked proof that the generic formula reproduces the app's existing literal convention exactly, once the `std` segment is correctly folded into `root` rather than modeled as a tree level.
- scenario:
  - when: the leaf `NAVCON > ATTACK PT` is resolved against this instance
  - then: the derived path is `compose_projects/bsg/resources/screen_base_layout/std/navcon/attack-pt.svg` — reproducing the literal `<root>/<mode>/<console-slug>/<subtab-slug>.svg` formula that motivated this spec (STD-screen-modeling-guidance.md), with `std` supplied by `root` and the remaining two levels supplied by the generic N-level join ([CXC-MENU-PATH])
- scenario:
  - when: `NAVCON > PLOT` has no `plot.svg` authored yet, but `std/navcon/default.svg` exists
  - then: `resolve` returns `std/navcon/default.svg` per [CXC-MENU-WALK] (ratified, [DEC-CXC-MENU-WALK-AMENDMENT-ADOPTED]); absent that too, it walks to `std/default.svg`, then the placeholder
- see-also: [CXC-MENU-SCHEMA], [CXC-MENU-PATH], [CXC-CIC-NAV], [CXC-COMP-STD-CONTENT], [CXC-COMP-KINDS], [CXC-CIC-RADIO-MODE]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-MENU]

### [CXC-MENU-CIC-INVENTORY] The STD 7x5 console/sub-tab inventory and its derived slugs

- definition: the STD mode's tree is exactly 7 consoles x 5 sub-tabs = 35 leaves, per `cic_menu_structure.md` (the current, authoritative markdown this instance's YAML supersedes). Every slug below is DERIVED by [CXC-MENU-SLUG]'s rule, shown here as a worked table, not a second source of truth — this table is the CONCRETE instance of [CXC-MENU-SLUG]'s abstract rule and of [CXC-MENU-PATH]'s abstract join.

| Console (slug) | Sub-tabs (label -> slug) |
|---|---|
| HELM (`helm`) | WAYPOINT->`waypoint`, HEADING->`heading`, TRACK->`track`, VELOCITY->`velocity`, FUEL->`fuel` |
| NAVCON (`navcon`) | CARTOGRAPHY->`cartography`, DEAD REC->`dead-rec`, PLOT->`plot`, TAC->`tac`, ATTACK PT->`attack-pt` |
| FTL (`ftl`) | PRM OUTPUT->`prm-output`, GENERATOR->`generator`, PROXIMITY->`proximity`, ALERTS->`alerts`, LOG->`log` (kind: pure-widget-no-file) |
| DC (`dc`) | OVERVIEW->`overview`, SYSTEMS->`systems`, SUBLIGHT->`sublight`, FLT DECKS->`flt-decks`, DISPATCH->`dispatch` (kind: pure-widget-no-file) |
| FIRE CONTROL (`fire-control`) | TARGETING->`targeting`, KEW->`kew`, S2SM->`s2sm`, NUCLEAR->`nuclear`, STORES->`stores` |
| EMSO (`emso`) | EA->`ea`, EWSP->`ewsp`, SIGINT->`sigint`, ELINT->`elint`, COMINT->`comint` |
| SECURITY (`security`) | OVERVIEW->`overview`, NETWORK->`network`, VTD->`vtd`, MARDET->`mardet`, DISPATCH->`dispatch` (kind: pure-widget-no-file) |

- default: every leaf not annotated `pure-widget-no-file` above defaults to `bespoke-svg`, per [CXC-COMP-KINDS]'s existing classification of the un-annotated majority (e.g. HELM+VELOCITY, NAVCON+CARTOGRAPHY).
- reserved-slug-check: no label in this table derives `default` — verified by inspection; [CXC-MENU-LINT]'s `reserved-slug` check has nothing to flag against the current 35.
- scenario:
